      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We recently introduced the ability to create and manage Amazon SageMaker Spaces on Amazon SageMaker HyperPod EKS clusters directly from the Amazon SageMaker Studio UI.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/manage-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod-spaces-directly-from-sagemaker-studio/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-06T15:47:02.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-13T06:32:25.112Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Earlier this year, we launched Amazon SageMaker Spaces for HyperPod , an add-on ML developers can use to create interactive development environments directly on HyperPod EKS clusters.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/manage-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod-spaces-directly-from-sagemaker-studio/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-06T15:47:02.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-13T06:32:25.112Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "With this new capability, data scientists can now create, configure, start, stop, and open Spaces directly from SageMaker Studio.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/manage-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod-spaces-directly-from-sagemaker-studio/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-06T15:47:02.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-13T06:32:25.112Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Figure 1: The IDE and Notebooks tab on the HyperPod cluster detail page shows all Spaces with their status, compute allocation, and quick actions to stop, open, or open in a remote IDE",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/manage-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod-spaces-directly-from-sagemaker-studio/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-06T15:47:02.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-13T06:32:25.112Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Administrators install the SageMaker Spaces add-on on their HyperPod EKS cluster using either the Quick install (one-click with optimized defaults) or Custom install option (required to set up web UI access) from their SageMaker HyperPod EKS cluster’s IDE and Notebooks tab.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/manage-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod-spaces-directly-from-sagemaker-studio/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-06T15:47:02.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-13T06:32:25.112Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Enable per-user identity propagation on the Studio domain: If your Studio domain was created before the SageMaker Studio and HyperPod Spaces integration was rolled out, you must enable per-user identity propagation to the HyperPod EKS cluster.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/manage-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod-spaces-directly-from-sagemaker-studio/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-06T15:47:02.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-13T06:32:25.112Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "After the add-on is installed and access is configured, data scientists navigate to their HyperPod cluster in SageMaker Studio under Compute → HyperPod and select the IDE and Notebooks tab to see the Spaces management interface (see Figure 1).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/manage-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod-spaces-directly-from-sagemaker-studio/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-06T15:47:02.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-13T06:32:25.112Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "You can also connect using the AWS Toolkit for Visual Studio Code, which lists your Spaces under SageMaker AI > HyperPod, and you can start, stop, and connect to Spaces directly from the toolkit panel.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/manage-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod-spaces-directly-from-sagemaker-studio/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-06T15:47:02.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-13T06:32:25.112Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "By default, SageMaker Spaces on HyperPod EKS clusters using Karpenter autoscaling incur a cold-start delay of 5–7 minutes the first time a Space is created on a scale-to-zero cluster, dominated by:",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/manage-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod-spaces-directly-from-sagemaker-studio/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-06T15:47:02.000Z",
